    "body": "Ukrainian drone manufacturer Skyfall shows its Vampire unmanned system at the Dubai Airshow on Nov. 19, 2025. (Daniel Woolfolk / Breaking Defense)\nWASHINGTON — American autonomous software firm Auterion and Ukrainian drone producer Skyfall plan to form a joint venture to “manufacture drones for Ukraine at high volume in a new factory in Germany,” Auterion announced today.\nThe new venture, called Skyfall X Auterion, “is being established under the auspices of the official ‘Build with Ukraine’ defense cooperation framework,” the announcement said.\nAccording to Auterion, “initial production” by the joint venture will “focus on the Shrike FPV platform” and is expected to later expand to Skyfall interceptors as well as middle- and deep-strike systems. “Every drone combines a Skyfall airframe with Auterion avionics” as well as Auterion’s operating system, the company said.\nAuterion and Skyfall previously partnered for drone production for Ukraine, but Auterion said today that a German factory in particular “adds production capacity outside the range of air strikes, while maintaining a knowledge link and short innovation cycle available to Skyfall’s engineers.\n“Feedback from units at the front reaches those engineers every week and goes straight into the German line,” the company said.\nAuterion, which is based in Munich as well as the US, said the agreement was inked during the German-Ukrainian Economic Forum today, and Reuters reported that the German government would provide funding for the new factory and for drone orders. Citing an industry official, the newswire reported the funding would be in the range of hundreds of millions of euros first to provide drones to Ukraine and then to the German armed forces.\n“SkyFall and Auterion have put more than 50,000 drones into the hands of Ukrainian units with advanced terminal guidance and target detection” Lorenz Meier, founder and CEO of Auterion, said in the announcement. “A factory in Germany gives German forces a domestic source for the same drones Ukrainian units rely on every week.”\nBreaking Defense Video\nCandidates are lining up to be the next top HASC Republican.\nWatch Now »\nThe real-world missile defense lessons from Ukraine and Iran — and how they matter for China\nWatch Now »\nA $1.1 trillion Pentagon budget plan sets up a fight on Capitol Hill\nWatch Now »\nThe Pentagon fails another audit. Can it turn things around by 2028?\nWatch Now »\nA new Air Force stunt plane, plus a shakeup for special operations\nWatch Now »\nNATO nations have a missile crisis. How did it happen, and can it be fixed?\nWatch Now »\nA Pentagon impeachment showdown, plus defense funding in limbo\nWatch Now »\npresented by\nThe push to give dismounted forces direct access to LEO and MEO networks [Sponsored]\nWatch Now »\nThe Pentagon wants a massive new military base. Where will it go?\nWatch Now »\nWhat now? Budget fight, Hegseth impeachment on deck for defense-focused lawmakers after midterms\nWatch Now »\nScroll for more video",
